    "raw_answer": "To determine the relative direction of the door, we can use the coordinates from the top view:\n\n* **Standing position (S) [Window]:** $(5.0, 9.5)$\n* **Facing position (F) [Telephone]:** $(4.5, 4.5)$\n* **Target position (T) [Door]:** $(0.5, 5.0)$\n\nFirst, we find the vectors relative to the standing position:\n* $\\vec{F} = F - S = (4.5 - 5.0, 4.5 - 9.5) = (-0.5, -5.0)$\n* $\\vec{T} = T - S = (0.5 - 5.0, 5.0 - 9.5) = (-4.5, -4.5)$\n\nNext, we calculate the cross product of $\\vec{F}$ and $\\vec{T}$ to determine if the door is to the left or right:\n$$\\text{cross}(\\vec{F}, \\vec{T}) = F_x T_y - F_y T_x$$\n$$\\text{cross}(\\vec{F}, \\vec{T}) = (-0.5 \\times -4.5) - (-5.0 \\times -4.5) = 2.25 - 22.5 = -20.25$$\n\nSince the cross product is negative, the door is to your right.\n\nANSWER: B",
